Z||000005||Chris Schaefer||12-28-2000||11:04 PM||||Just under two years ago I installed a '92 3.4L DOHC V6 in my car.  I used the motor and transmition mounts from Chris West.  Also I used two left or right side exhaust manifolds (I can't remember which) as to plum the exhaust the same as a stock V6.  The wiring was done by using a Fiero tech manual and a '92 Grand Prix tech manual.  I cut the '92 wiring harness and rewired it through the Fiero fire wall then wired into the '92 ECM.  I had to add a few wires due to the newer motor.<P>In all everything just bolted right together.  I have talked with 2 other DOHC owners.  One used the Auto trans for the motor and the other used the stock 5spd.  I was told that the clutch to use was for a stock "Z" Berretta.<P>I like the way my car runs.  I have owned a '88 5.0L Mustang and my Fiero feels to run about as fast, not bad for a Fiero.  It is not the fasted Fiero but it sure does move well.  I have never run a measured 0-60 but if I had to guess I would say it would get there in about 5.8 seconds.||||reg||2
